    {
      "check_id": "W7B8:W7B8:CHK-0164",
      "checklist_item": {
        "check_id": "W7B8:W7B8:CHK-0164",
        "property_id": "PROP-W5B14-31",
        "title": "Verify Trust Boundary Integrity for tb-001: Does compute_cells_and_kzg_proofs strictly enforce BYTES_PER_BLOB input size and produce exactly CELLS_PER_EXT_BLOB cells and proofs?",
        "severity": "Medium",
        "mindset": "Boundary Guard",
        "is_boundary_check": true,
        "reachability": {
          "classification": "external-reachable",
          "entry_points": [
            "Transaction"
          ],
          "attacker_controlled": true,
          "validation_layers": [
            "Transaction validation",
            "Blob size check"
          ],
          "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope",
          "notes": "A blob submitter provides blob bytes via type-3 transaction. Incorrect blob size must be rejected before polynomial operations."
        },
        "test_procedure": "1. Locate the compute_cells_and_kzg_proofs function (SG-020) in the codebase.\n2. Identify the input validation check for blob size: MUST be exactly BYTES_PER_BLOB (131072 bytes for EIP-4844).\n3. CRITICAL: Verify this size check occurs BEFORE any polynomial conversion or cell computation begins.\n4. Design boundary crossing tests for undersized blobs:\n   (a) blob size = 0 bytes (empty blob)\n   (b) blob size = 1 byte (minimal non-empty)\n   (c) blob size = BYTES_PER_BLOB - 1 (off-by-one short)\n   (d) blob size = BYTES_PER_BLOB / 2 (half size)\n   (e) blob size = 31 bytes (one field element minus one byte)\n5. Design boundary crossing tests for oversized blobs:\n   (a) blob size = BYTES_PER_BLOB + 1 (off-by-one long)\n   (b) blob size = BYTES_PER_BLOB + 32 (one extra field element)\n   (c) blob size = BYTES_PER_BLOB * 2 (double size)\n   (d) blob size = MAX_UINT64 (extreme overflow attempt)\n6. Verify output cardinality invariant:\n   (a) Check that CELLS_PER_EXT_BLOB cells are always produced for valid input\n   (b) Check that CELLS_PER_EXT_BLOB proofs are always produced for valid input\n   (c) Verify cells array length == proofs array length\n   (d) For EIP-4844/Fusaka: CELLS_PER_EXT_BLOB = 128\n7. Test the validation layer ordering:\n   (a) Does transaction validation check blob size first?\n   (b) If transaction validation is bypassed (e.g., via internal API), does compute_cells_and_kzg_proofs still validate?\n   (c) Trace call paths from transaction ingestion to compute_cells_and_kzg_proofs\n8. Attack vector analysis:\n   (a) Can an attacker craft a type-3 transaction with malformed blob size?\n   (b) Can RLP encoding tricks bypass length validation?\n   (c) Are there any blob size fields that could be inconsistent (declared vs actual)?\n9. Impact assessment if validation is missing:\n   (a) Undersized blob: polynomial conversion would read garbage or crash on out-of-bounds access\n   (b) Oversized blob: extra bytes ignored OR buffer overflow in polynomial conversion\n   (c) Wrong cell count: downstream consumers (validators, data availability sampling) would receive corrupted data\n10. Cross-reference with blob_to_polynomial (SG-018):\n    (a) Verify SG-018 also enforces BYTES_PER_BLOB constraint\n    (b) Check for defense-in-depth: multiple validation layers\n11. Verify error handling:\n    (a) Invalid blob size MUST return a clear error, not crash\n    (b) Error must be deterministic across implementations\n    (c) Check for panic/exception paths that could cause node denial-of-service\n12. Check CELLS_PER_EXT_BLOB constant usage:\n    (a) Is it hardcoded or derived from FIELD_ELEMENTS_PER_EXT_BLOB / FIELD_ELEMENTS_PER_CELL?\n    (b) Verify consistency across all references\n    (c) For Fusaka: CELLS_PER_EXT_BLOB = 128 (8192 / 64)\n13. Fuzz testing recommendation:\n    (a) Generate random blob sizes near BYTES_PER_BLOB boundary\n    (b) Generate blobs with valid size but corrupted content\n    (c) Test concurrent blob submissions with mixed valid/invalid sizes\n14. Verify the pre-condition from invariant SG-020:INV-002 is enforced at the trust boundary (tb-001) before any processing occurs.\n15. PoC requirement: demonstrate a blob that bypasses size validation and causes incorrect polynomial representation or cell count.",
        "bug_class": "Input Validation / Trust Boundary Enforcement",
        "risk_category": "Tampering",
        "notes": "Source: PROP-W5B14-31, Invariant: SG-020:INV-002, Trust Boundary: tb-001, Primary Element: SG-020:compute_cells_and_kzg_proofs, Covered Nodes: actor-blob-submitter, actor-block-proposer. This is a BOUNDARY PROPERTY where external blob submitters provide untrusted data via type-3 transactions. The validation must occur at the trust boundary before polynomial operations begin. Two critical invariants: (1) input blob MUST be exactly BYTES_PER_BLOB, (2) output MUST contain exactly CELLS_PER_EXT_BLOB cells and proofs. A successful bypass could cause incorrect polynomial representations, leading to invalid KZG proofs or data availability sampling failures. Bug bounty eligible - requires PoC demonstrating size validation bypass.",
